
# flux nexus, research, library (0.9.0)
tile.fluxecho.nexus.name=Flux Nexus
fluxecho.nexus.tip=§3The nexus pinned into the flux layer: research, manifestation and modules start here§r\nDraws its upkeep from the team wireless network\nFormed: white ribs hold white rings, the core floats in the middle, a beam runs up into the sky
fluxecho.nexus.place_hint=§7Right-click the ground: the core goes two blocks up, and the nexus surveys, projects and, once you press Start, builds itself§r\n§7Place it sneaking: just the core, built by hand the 0.9.2 way§r
fluxecho.nexus.carries_credit=§bCarries build credit§r: %s materials, %s parts, %s kinds from the recycle store
fluxecho.nexus.carries_pending=§bCarries an unfinished manifestation§r: %s × %s
fluxecho.nexus.carries_campus=§bCarries its campus§r: put it back where it stood (%s) and the campus carries on
fluxecho.nexus.carries_overflow=§bAnother %s kinds from the recycle store§r are kept for your team: they come back into the recycle store of your team's nexus as it has room
fluxecho.nexus.structure=§bPhase I: an 11×11 octagonal base, 6 high§r\n· Base: Flux Frame Base, the eight spokes Lit Frame Base\n· Middle: three Flux Conduits, a Crystal Seat on top\n· The four diagonals: Frame Pillars, 2 high three blocks out, then 2 high one block further in (white ribs, solid once formed too)\n· Layer 6: a ring of 16 Ring Segments\n· The core sits on the front rim of the base, two blocks above it (a Console Stand under it), facing out\n· Each later phase adds a stage on top: pillars, conduits, a seat, a ring; from phase II the middle of the base is a Light Lift Pad (the nexus grows itself once the phase is researched)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it\nNEI preview: tiers 1–5 are phases I–V, 6–10 the same with the city standing round it, each building of the phase on its site
